(6034325, 858010, 42495, '<td valign="top">Very cool, I missed this during the competition.  I think it''s much stronger than the original.</td>', 'Very cool, I missed this during the competition.  I think it''s much stronger than the original.', '2010-06-01 00:55:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(6066387, 857081, 68947, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot and I agree with Melethia that you have a "target audience" of which, I''m one for this shot.  I actually gave you a 9 on this one because it spoke volumes to me.  The bike, to me, seemed as though it might have been brought into the area by someone who had either stolen it or, was in the area for some other reason that would not normally be "his/her area" so to speak.  I wasn''t bothered by that.  I think though that DPC is simply geared towards a different style of photography...more the advertising/stock shot combo, eye candy and a very smooth, pretty, studio look or beautiful landscape/waterscape/skyscape type of scene (zoo shots work really well in here as do water splashes and bees ROFL! ;))  Frankly, I love this type of shot and thus, the 9 in score from me.  Sorry that I didn''t have time to comment sooner than this. Better late than never though. :)</td>', 'This is a great shot and I agree with Melethia that you have a "target audience" of which, I''m one for this shot.  I actually gave you a 9 on this one because it spoke volumes to me.  The bike, to me, seemed as though it might have been brought into the area by someone who had either stolen it or, was in the area for some other reason that would not normally be "his/her area" so to speak.  I wasn''t bothered by that.  I think though that DPC is simply geared towards a different style of photography...more the advertising/stock shot combo, eye candy and a very smooth, pretty, studio look or beautiful landscape/waterscape/skyscape type of scene (zoo shots work really well in here as do water splashes and bees ROFL! ;))  Frankly, I love this type of shot and thus, the 9 in score from me.  Sorry that I didn''t have time to comment sooner than this. Better late than never though. :)', '2010-06-22 21:38:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(6068161, 857898, 100831, '<td valign="top">love the title!</td>', 'love the title!', '2010-06-23 20:09:46.000000', NULL, 0),
